# Hostinger shared hosting serves Node.js apps via Apache + Phusion Passenger
# in front of the app (LiteSpeed in Apache-compatible mode). Without this file,
# Apache tries to resolve every request (including client-side SPA routes like
# /staff/abc123) as a static file under this directory, finds nothing, and
# serves a 404/blank response instead of handing the request to the Node
# process — which is why the URL changes on click but the page stays blank.
#
# IMPORTANT — before relying on this file:
# 1. Check hPanel's Node.js application settings (or File Manager) for an
#    EXISTING .htaccess at the app's actual document root. hPanel normally
#    auto-generates one from the "Application Root" / "Application Startup
#    File" fields when you create the Node.js app there. If one already
#    exists, reconcile with it instead of letting this file silently
#    conflict — don't deploy both blindly.
# 2. Replace REPLACE_WITH_APP_ROOT_ABSOLUTE_PATH below with the real absolute
#    path hPanel assigned this app (visible in hPanel's Node.js app details,
#    e.g. /home/<hostinger-username>/domains/<yourdomain>/...). I have no way
#    to know this value from the repo or this session — a wrong path here
#    will stop the app from starting at all, so do not leave it unset.
# 3. PassengerStartupFile below assumes this repo's build output layout
#    (.output/server/index.mjs, produced by `bun run build` / `npm run
#    build` with the node-server Nitro preset) and that PassengerAppRoot is
#    the repository root — adjust if hPanel's app root points somewhere else.

PassengerNodejs /usr/bin/node
PassengerAppRoot REPLACE_WITH_APP_ROOT_ABSOLUTE_PATH
PassengerAppType node
PassengerStartupFile .output/server/index.mjs

RewriteEngine On

# Serve real static files (the built JS/CSS/image assets in this folder)
# directly instead of proxying them to Node.
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} -f
RewriteRule ^ - [L]

# Everything else — including client-side SPA routes with no matching file
# on disk — goes to the Node app.
RewriteRule ^$ http://internal/ [P,L]
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ http://internal/$1 [P,L]
